s deemed significant for serving Austin during the early 20th century, a period of renewed growth and development."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0146-6f444170c228:d04", "start": 503, "end": 638, "text": "The building was transferred to the local Knights of Pythias chapter and has since been used for various community events and meetings."}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0146-6f444170c228:d05", "start": 0, "end": 150, "text": "Austin City Hall (Austin, Texas) Austin City Hall is the seat of Austin municipal government, located at 301 W 2nd St in downtown Austin, Texas (USA)."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0146-6f444170c228:d05", "start": 151, "end": 194, "text": "The current building was completed in 2004."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0146-6f444170c228:d05", "start": 195, "end": 257, "text": "Austin formerly operated its City Hall at 124 West 8th Street."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0146-6f444170c228:d05", "start": 258, "end": 532, "text": "Antoine Predock and Cotera + Reed Architects designed a new city hall building, which was intended to reflect what \"The Dallas Morning News\" referred to as a “crazy-quilt vitality, that embraces everything from country music to environmental protests and high-tech swagger.”"}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0146-6f444170c228:d05", "start": 533, "end": 614, "text": "The new city hall, built from recycled materials, has solar panels in its garage."}, "D6S6": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0146-6f444170c228:d05", "start": 615, "end": 618, "text": "The"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0146-6f444170c228:d06", "start": 0, "end": 222, "text": "'s Mansion Treaty Oak UFCU Disch-Falk Field University of Texas Tower Zach Theatre History 1839 city plan 1928 city plan Austin Dam failure Capitol View Corridors COVID-19 pandemic French Legation Greater Austin Stephen F."}, "D7S2": {"